Grammar

Rule 0     S' -> Program
Rule 1     Program -> Type ID ( ) Block
Rule 2     Block -> { Declarations Statements }
Rule 3     Declarations -> Declarations Declaration
Rule 4     Declarations -> empty
Rule 5     Declaration -> Type ID ;
Rule 6     Type -> INT
Rule 7     Type -> FLOAT
Rule 8     Type -> VOID
Rule 9     Statements -> Statements Statement
Rule 10    Statements -> empty
Rule 11    Statement -> Assignment
Rule 12    Assignment -> ID = Expression ;
Rule 13    Expression -> Relation
Rule 14    Relation -> Relation + Term
Rule 15    Relation -> Term
Rule 16    Term -> Term * Factor
Rule 17    Term -> Factor
Rule 18    Factor -> INTLIT
Rule 19    Factor -> ID
Rule 20    Factor -> ( Expression )
Rule 21    empty -> <empty>

Terminals, with rules where they appear

(                    : 1 20
)                    : 1 20
*                    : 16
+                    : 14
;                    : 5 12
=                    : 12
FLOAT                : 7
ID                   : 1 5 12 19
INT                  : 6
INTLIT               : 18
VOID                 : 8
error                : 
{                    : 2
}                    : 2

Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

Assignment           : 11
Block                : 1
Declaration          : 3
Declarations         : 2 3
Expression           : 12 20
Factor               : 16 17
Program              : 0
Relation             : 13 14
Statement            : 9
Statements           : 2 9
Term                 : 14 15 16
Type                 : 1 5
empty                : 4 10

